c", "title": "Policy and regulation", "children": [{"id": "cae0150d-c2fb-4e45-babc-9e74f8a74ae2", "type": "concept", "title": "Antitrust and collusion"}, {"id": "bd569a1d-5176-431f-a7fa-5eef6175ed00", "type": "concept", "title": "Entry deterrence"}, {"id": "5ffed404-c6da-420f-ac70-c518be434b38", "type": "concept", "title": "Regulatory mechanism design"}], "description": "Game theory helps evaluate market power, collusion, and institutional rules."}]}, {"id": "bc505ca6-5e0b-46c9-9509-17c7ed55b687", "type": "topic", "title": "Evolutionary, Learning, Behavioral, and Experimental Games", "description": "Study how strategies emerge through adaptation, bounded rationality, experiments, and social preferences.", "children": [{"id": "18ca5bbb-fbbf-4057-8739-557ee065b3b6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evolutionary games", "children": [{"id": "0cdd4be6-2aaa-4bee-bccf-8f325307bfce", "type": "concept", "title": "Evolutionarily stable strategies"}, {"id": "7042f517-7fbc-4da2-9b2d-698ee42c2608", "type": "concept", "title": "Replicator dynamics"}, {"id": "027d5882-a6fb-42cd-9230-5d51ecab6c37", "type": "concept", "title": "Hawk-dove and coordination examples"}], "description": "Evolutionary models study strategy survival through adaptation rather than full rational calculation."}, {"id": "d2ea9d59-9f3b-40b1-acc4-4d6bdd8dd97b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Learning in games", "children": [{"id": "07484054-f79e-4bf6-aba5-bf4dd3adf356", "type": "concept", "title": "Fictitious play"}, {"id": "10061d12-6568-4fee-8cb9-b815cccd3169", "type": "concept", "title": "Reinforcement learning intuition"}, {"id": "34f64fc9-71af-45ae-af68-fb4d2faff3f7", "type": "concept", "title": "Best-response dynamics"}], "description": "Players may learn through experience, feedback, and adjustment."}, {"id": "5ef32c7f-ee79-4d35-a365-e8de44f9cec0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Behavioral and experimental evidence", "children": [{"id": "403f6c5e-55a0-4825-bfab-70879bc77745", "type": "concept", "title": "Ultimatum and dictator games"}, {"id": "162b4e1b-5c58-4405-b16e-a79be2f7cffd", "type": "concept", "title": "Public-goods experiments"}, {"id": "891151b4-30ba-49b5-9c79-a8adeb4d33d3", "type": "concept", "title": "Level-k and cognitive hierarchy models"}], "description": "Experiments reveal fairness, reciprocity, bounded rationality, and systematic deviations from narrow payoff maximization."}]}, {"id": "035c084f-64ae-477e-9619-dcc7c4587e89", "type": "topic", "title": "Network, Matching, and Computational Game Theory", "description": "Extend strategic analysis to networks, matching markets, algorithms, and computational complexity.", "children": [{"id": "0be01a9a-e4a9-436f-8255-1cf9cbe686b3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Network games", "children": [{"id": "8dc054ca-85c3-41ee-b983-252b0e6afd53", "type": "concept", "title": "Strategic complements and substitutes"}, {"id": "6bb11eb6-a3d9-4ee7-8c63-5d340997e56a", "type": "concept", "title": "Diffusion and cascades"}, {"id": "3306499a-b82b-45f9-876c-bb4e8b1c3ff5", "type": "concept", "title": "Peer effects"}], "description": "Networks shape who interacts with whom and how local incentives produce aggregate outcomes."}, {"id": "eeff20c6-7d2f-4bd9-936a-db9855345ee8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Matching markets", "children": [{"id": "efe81eff-a11d-4d03-8860-8d2e5d83a696", "type": "concept", "title": "Stable matching"}, {"id": "e7ec3a16-42c1-4ee5-80fa-802397a129bd", "type": "concept", "title": "Deferred acceptance"}, {"id": "cfe12704-d4fb-48d5-8e8d-c480f5bf02c5", "type": "concept", "title": "School choice and labor matching"}], "description": "Matching theory studies allocation without prices or with constrained prices."}, {"id": "7d45bff8-f163-49cf-8d92-83e4a2ec6f5e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Computational game theory", "children": [{"id": "caa4df67-2471-4b88-ad96-a22b0874c002", "type": "concept", "title": "Complexity of equilibrium computation"}, {"id": "51289daf-3c57-47b2-86ef-73d4bb194d4b", "type": "concept", "title": "Algorithmic mechanism design"}, {"id": "422f7e79-d070-4e97-a59e-98bae193b3a8", "type": "concept", "title": "Multi-agent systems and no-regret learning"}], "description": "Modern applications often require algorithmic equilibrium and mechanism analysis."}]}, {"id": "5ff58ce1-73c5-45d3-8f51-5de6257d877e", "type": "topic", "title": "Empirical, Quantitative, and Capstone Strategic Analysis", "description": "Use data, computation, and a complete case project to turn game-theoretic models into defensible analysis.", "children": [{"id": "b9d9339d-e214-4e4e-8a7a-d25ba102a408", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Model calibration and simulation", "children": [{"id": "1b3f9095-2718-495e-a993-ca6e12836da7", "type": "concept", "title": "Payoff estimation"}, {"id": "1df31693-eb3a-4da8-8841-6150ae1e1351", "type": "concept", "title": "Sensitivity analysis"}, {"id": "d4167be3-6723-4fcb-bbd0-6d0f658eef1f", "type": "concept", "title": "Agent-based simulation preview"}], "description": "Students learn to test strategic intuitions numerically before claiming insight."}, {"id": "79917721-ccc8-4151-8b43-a669ea91ff34", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Empirical game theory", "children": [{"id": "5834281d-f141-44b1-af8b-acd820f3d2e0", "type": "concept", "title": "Structural estimation intuition"}, {"id": "7ee87733-0573-4d2b-8a57-133cf05f6030", "type": "concept", "title": "Experimental data"}, {"id": "4211fc0f-ed09-4c8a-b754-6af857abbdf8", "type": "concept", "title": "Field evidence and natural experiments"}], "description": "Data can discipline assumptions about beliefs, strategies, and market structure."}, {"id": "b3fa7bc0-fa3f-484c-a5ec-65a48a124f4d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Capstone case", "children": [{"id": "5db7385c-ffd6-44ea-b602-72bde1d7dca7", "type": "concept", "title": "Game description and payoffs"}, {"id": "dfc5a4d0-6645-49e7-a981-b00a3560807c", "type": "concept", "title": "Equilibrium analysis and robustness"}, {"id": "245fb62f-abfa-4c3c-8070-93ca89ad84cf", "type": "concept", "